sequenceDiagram
accTitle: Local writes replicate asynchronously
accDescr: A local write is acknowledged before another Region necessarily sees it, after replication the remote read returns the event.
participant A as API in Region A
participant DA as Replica A
participant DB as Replica B
participant B as API in Region B
A->>DA: Write unique event E
DA-->>A: Write succeeds
B->>DB: Read event E immediately
DB-->>B: E may not yet be visible
DA-->>DB: Managed asynchronous replication
B->>DB: Read event E later
DB-->>B: Event E
